<title>SRI LANKA: Distilleries rises despite duty hike.</title>
<headline>Distilleries rises despite duty hike.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Distilleries Company of Sri Lanka Ltd rose 7.7 percent, or 50 cents, to seven rupees, on turnover of 571,000 shares, as investors shrugged off a 10 percent duty hike on hard liquor in the budget for fiscal 1997, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The company, which has the major share of the local market for alcohol, is going to hardly feel the impact,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
